            <ArticleTitle>Cocaine-related maternal death.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hemodynamic overload, cardiac ischemia, and arrhythmia are postulated to originate from &quot;sex-cocaine&quot; syndrome resulting in maternal and fetal death. High concentrations of cocaine and metabolites in maternal blood, urine, and nasal secretions confirmed recent ingestion. Changes in the maternal life-style may have contributed to the poor pregnancy outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
